    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW29V3UomkqehSCVSRkTj1Bkq)_\n\n## What\nImproves #280: when the `crossref`'ed entry has no literature note, `bib-parent` is no longer left out. The note is made and linked.\n- The parent is matched by its citation key (the `ROAM_REFS` key), never by title.\n- A missing parent is made without asking, by `sp-litnotes-meta-create-function`, the same path `sp-litnotes-meta-backfill-children` and `-all-children` use:\n  - `vulpea-create` with an ID, `:CREATED:`, `ROAM_REFS`, the `litnote` tag and the BibTeX type tag (`sp-bibtex-types`)\n  - filled from its own BibTeX entry, given a plain title, and put in the Vulpea database\n- `sp-litnotes-meta-fill` (single) and `sp-litnotes-meta-fill-all-convert` (batch from #348) both do this.\n- Batch: each missing parent is made once, however many notes cross-reference it (`sp-litnotes-meta--made-parents`). It is counted in the one-time questions and in the final message.\n- Dry run: new \"Parent notes to make\" section (each parent once, with the notes that link it), a count line, and \"(new note)\" on the `bib-parent` lines.\n- Deep chains are flagged and avoided:\n  - A normal crossref is `child -> parent` and the parent has no crossref. `child -> parent -> grandparent` (loops and self-references included) is flagged.\n  - For such a note the fill and the batch convert nothing: no `bib-parent`, no parent note, even if the parent already has a note.\n  - The dry run has a count line and a section \"Crossref chains deeper than two levels\" listing each chain; the single command prints a message.\n  - New `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-fill-deep-chain` converts one flagged note on purpose: it shows the chain, asks once, fills the note and links or makes its direct parent. The parent is filled by the normal rules, so a loop is cut there. There is no batch version.\n- A parent key with no BibTeX entry is left out with a message.\n- `sp-litnotes-meta-offer-parent` became `sp-litnotes-meta-create-parent` (default t, old name kept as an obsolete alias). Set it to nil to get the old \"leave it out\" behaviour. The `y-or-n-p` question and the `citar-create-note` route are gone.\n\n## Tests\n- 37 tests in `tests/sp-litnotes-meta-test.el` pass in Emacs 29 (the old \"offer to create\" test was replaced by new ones):\n  - parent made silently and filled, linked, not made again on a second run\n  - existing parent not made; option off leaves the line out\n  - deep chains (loop, self-reference, parent with a note) make nothing; detection of one-hop chains\n  - the dry run lists a parent once for two children and flags a chain; the convert makes a parent once and converts nothing for a chain\n  - `sp-litnotes-meta-fill-deep-chain`: declined, converted (makes `b` then `c`), loop cut at the parent, refuses a normal note\n- Literate doc `docs/tangles/academic/sp-litnotes-meta.org` updated as bullet lists; it tangles to the committed `.el`.\n- Not run on the real vault or in Emacs 31.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits, per the nightly-tidy rule.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiD5W4k4UTcudsexBjX",
